    Remove whitespace from @Path parameter declarations (#8243)
    
    JAX-RS ignores whitespace around the name and regular expression of a
    path parameter, but the REST docs do not. RestDocData.isValidPath()
    rejects such paths, which makes the whole REST docs page of the UI
    configuration service fail with an HTTP 500:
    
        Path '/{component}/{filename : .+}' must not be null and must look
        something like /a/b/{c}.
    
    The placeholder handling of the docs testing form would not recognize
    these parameters either.
    
    Remove the whitespace from all such declarations. The endpoints behave
    exactly as before.
    
    Fixes #8242
    
